module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "rc_list_concat appends a small right side element by element and keeps im Vector append for large right sides, with the threshold measured, SUFFICIENT FOR gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder concat_chain to double linearly on the emitted path, and a control that times that arm across doublings and goes red when the ratio leaves the linear band."
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a sequence built by repeatedly appending a small right side onto a growing left side costs more than linear time in the number of appends. std.algebra non_empty_append realizes its tail as list_append(list_snoc_item(left.tail, right.head), right.tail), and list_append lowers to v1_rt rc_list_concat, which is make_mut(a).append(b.clone()) on an im Vector (v1.compiler.runtime_rust rt_rc_container_ops).",
    "HARM: an accumulator over FreeMonoid or FreeSemigroup pays a cost that grows faster than its length, on the emitted Rust path and in the v1 interpreter. Fold accumulators already call non_empty_append on non-text sequences (std.generated_provider group_provider_demands, gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge runner_host_cap_pending_reloads, gunbc.host.host_converge slice_control_plan_of), so far on small n. The A4(a) NonEmptyStr cut would route every migrated text accumulator through the same append, so the defect blocks that cut (operator ruling 2026-10-23: no cut and no generator until the cause is found and fixed).",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, AND WHICH PART EACH SOURCE ESTABLISHES. The arms are gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder, one per link. The label //gunbc/instruments:append-chain-ladder re-derives only that every arm builds the element count it owes at n = 1000, 2000 and 4000; it reports no time. The CURVE below was read by an out-of-band timing run on srv1, 2026-10-23, not by the label: the main seed at 08437488ec1 (bin 0d1af18c) emitted the arms to Rust, each was timed best-of-5 over doubling n from 2000 to 32000 in one build-and-run dispatch, and gunbc run timed the interpreter arms from 1000 to 8000 or 16000. The timing rows and their ratio-threshold fold are a DECLARED FRONTIER of the same label, sunny-bee-153's list-concat-linearity control, triggered by the rc_list_concat fix landing: until that extension lands, the curve is a transcribed reading of that run, not a re-derivable one. push_chain (list_snoc_item alone) doubles linearly. concat_chain (list_append alone, fixed 8-element right side) does not: its ratio per doubling rises toward 4. elementwise_chain (the same right side appended one element at a time) doubles linearly. non_empty_append_chain follows concat_chain. The same split holds on the emitted path and in the interpreter. concat_chain and elementwise_chain append the same 8-element right side, through list_append and through one list_snoc_item per element. One is superlinear and the other linear, so the growth is carried by the list_append realization, rc_list_concat over im::Vector::append. The mechanism inside it is not isolated: the two arms also differ in their make_mut and clone pattern, so this row makes no claim about aliasing or make_mut.",
    "CAUSE, MEASURED NOT EXPLAINED: the earliest unjustified boundary is rc_list_concat, which realizes every append, including a small right side onto a large left, as im Vector append. The mechanism inside im is not examined; the concat_chain / elementwise_chain pair locates the growth in the list_append realization (rc_list_concat over im::Vector::append), not which part of it. The interpreter realizes list_append through its own route and shows the same curve; under the v1 freeze that path gets no performance work and is recorded here only.",
    "CEILING: mechanically preventable, through a control that times concat_chain across doublings. Construction is not available: the carrier admits the append, and its cost is a property of the realization. No control observes append cost today, so reverting a fix would leave every committed test green.",
    "RECEIPT, D13 whole-pool census (session calm-ferret-416): in the emitted census binary, v1_rt rc_list_concat paid a per-call cost nearly independent of the right side's length, so build_adjacency_views (one concat(acc, [x]) per edge) paid it per edge. The landed rule is narrow and states no crossover: a singleton right side is pushed, an empty right side returns the left, an empty left side takes the right whole, and anything else keeps the im Vector append (authority v1.compiler.runtime_rust rt_rc_container_ops and rt_collection_ops, mirrored in the checked-in seed and v1_rt.rs; the three-file agreement is pinned by runtime_rust_seed_bootstrap_sync_witness). Controls: append_agrees_with_extension_for_every_shape (value agreement over every shape) and an_empty_side_copies_no_element (no element is cloned on an empty side). No crossover is claimed for right sides of two or more elements; that needs the timing control. RUNG UNCHANGED: Mitigatable. No control times the arm across doublings, so a revert of the singleton push leaves value tests green; the named next trigger is the append_chain_ladder concat_chain timing frontier. OPEN FOLLOW-UP, INTERPRETER TWIN: claim_batch shows the same curve through its own list-append route, with eval_steps exactly 2.0x because the cost is inside the primitive; under the v1 freeze it gets no performance work here.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.runtime_rust", decl_name: "rt_rc_container_ops"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "non_empty_append"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "list_append"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "push_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "concat_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "elementwise_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "non_empty_append_chain"),
  ],
}
